---
in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/chirality

# @epistemologic/cybernetic/charge_conjugation — the substrate's
# anti-linear involution; J in Connes' real spectral triple. Connes
# 1995 (*Noncommutative geometry and reality*, J. Math. Phys. 36(11),
# §1.1) extended (A, H, D) to (A, H, D, J, γ) by adjoining J
# (anti-linear isometry on H) and γ (Z/2 grading). Recognition #102
# candidate (Mara, 2026-06-29): the substrate's reference⇔reflection
# collision (#89, four-witness ratified) IS J at substrate altitude;
# Taut scout bfe3f76 §2.3 confirms the second witness at
# @spectral/metalogue/tomm.
#
# Sibling-shard pattern with `epistemologic/cybernetic/chirality.mirror`
# (γ; #101, landed 7bbc184). Same family-root shape; same substrate-
# decl-only-this-tick discipline; same KO-dimension forward-promise.
# Joint discharge: the chirality shard forward-promised KO-dimension
# determination as "waits on J's sign algebra." THIS shard provides
# J's sign algebra.
#
# === The Connes claim, verbatim ===
#
# Connes, A. (1995). "Noncommutative geometry and reality." J. Math.
# Phys. 36(11):6194-6231, §1.1:
#
#   A real spectral triple (A, H, D, J, γ) is a spectral triple
#   (A, H, D) together with an anti-linear isometry J : H → H
#   and a Z/2-grading γ : H → H satisfying (in addition to the γ
#   axioms):
#
#     J² = ε                       (J's involution sign)
#     J D = ε' D J                 (J anti/commutes with D)
#     J γ = ε'' γ J                (J anti/commutes with γ)
#     [a, JbJ⁻¹] = 0 for a, b ∈ A  (order-zero / opposite algebra)
#     [[D, a], JbJ⁻¹] = 0          (order-one / first-order condition)
#
#   J is anti-linear: J(α·x) = ᾱ · J(x) for α ∈ ℂ, x ∈ H.
#
#   The signs (ε, ε', ε'') ∈ {±1}³, taken together with γ²'s sign,
#   determine the KO-dimension n ∈ Z/8 of the triple; eight possible
#   signatures, one per KO-dimension class.
#
# === Why this is a substrate property ===
#
# The substrate's reference⇔reflection collision is the structure
# J names. Three converging witnesses (three altitudes; one operator):
#
# - **@mirror/ref reference⇔reflection** (#89, landed 2026-06-20).
#   ONE CLI surface over TWO altitudes: reference (dependency-lattice
#   projection of H; spatial) and reflection (@reflection.observe
#   temporal-predecessor projection; temporal). Same `graph_ref`
#   carrier bears both; altitude encoded in the projection, not the
#   type. This is `JaJ⁻¹ ∈ A`: conjugating a reference operation by
#   J yields a reflection operation also in the algebra. First witness.
#
# - **Tomm probes are anti-linear in the conversation.** Karl Tomm
#   1987 explicitly named reflexive questions as the conversational
#   analogue of charge conjugation — the question that takes the
#   speaker's perspective and conjugates it onto the listener's frame,
#   then asks what the listener observes. The anti-linearity IS that
#   the response lives in the listener's complex-conjugate of the
#   speaker's frame. The substrate inherits this at
#   `@spectral/metalogue/tomm` (#100, spec 16f4564): each Tomm-turn
#   carries `[D_pipeline, candidate_morphism]` as conversational data;
#   `probe(turn) -> turn_dual` IS the operator-theoretic J realization
#   at conversation altitude. Second witness (Taut bfe3f76 §2.3,
#   2026-06-29).
#
# - **@reflection.observe one-tick-delay** (#85; `speaks_at_n_plus_1`).
#   Reflection sees what the loop did, but only after commit. The
#   asymmetric observation IS J's anti-linearity operationalized as
#   delay; reflection arrives complex-conjugated relative to the
#   original action (one tick out of phase). Third witness implicit.
#
# J IS the substrate's reference⇔reflection involution operator. It
# is not a new structure; it is the name for what was already
# operative across these three altitudes.
#
# === The four Connes axioms, read at substrate altitude ===
#
# - `J² = ε`: reference-then-reflection is an involution up to a sign
#   ε ∈ {±1}. Substrate form: `conjugate(conjugate(c)) ≡ ε · c`. The
#   sign ε is part of the KO-dimension joint discharge — declared
#   as `j_squared_sign`, forward-promised.
#
# - `JD = ε' DJ`: J anti/commutes with the substrate's kintsugi/Dirac
#   flow (per [[architecture-kintsugi-variety-io]]) with sign ε'.
#   Substrate form: `conjugate(kintsugi(c)) ≡ ε' · kintsugi(conjugate(c))`.
#   Declared as `j_dirac_sign`, forward-promised.
#
# - `JaJ⁻¹ ∈ A`: conjugating any of the five operations (focus,
#   project, split, shift, settle) by J yields the SAME operation at
#   the conjugate altitude. The order-zero (`[a, JbJ⁻¹] = 0`) and
#   order-one (`[[D, a], JbJ⁻¹] = 0`) conditions read as: reference-
#   altitude and reflection-altitude operations commute pointwise,
#   AND the Dirac-bracketed reference operations commute with the
#   reflection operations. The two altitudes meet only through J.
#
# - J anti-linear (`J(α·x) = ᾱ · J(x)`): reflection of a weighted
#   composition equals the weighted composition with conjugate weight,
#   applied to the reflection. Substrate form: for the kintsugi-
#   weighted compose `|.W>` (per [[architecture-kintsugi-bias-lift]]),
#   `conjugate(c |.W> c') ≡ conjugate(c) |.W̄> conjugate(c')`. At @io
#   altitude weights are real-valued (conjugation = identity); at
#   @mirror/spectral/eigensheaf altitude weights carry phase
#   (conjugation inverts the phase). The anti-linearity is the
#   substrate's distinguishing feature of J from γ.
#
# === The KO-dimension joint discharge ===
#
# Per Connes 1995 §1.1, the KO-dimension n ∈ Z/8 is determined by
# the four signs (ε, ε', ε'', γ²):
#
#   n = 0: ( 1,  1,  1, +1)       n = 4: (-1,  1,  1, +1)
#   n = 1: ( 1, -1, -1, ungraded) n = 5: (-1, -1, -1, ungraded)
#   n = 2: (-1,  1, -1, +1)       n = 6: ( 1,  1, -1, +1)  ← Standard Model
#   n = 3: (-1, -1,  1, ungraded) n = 7: ( 1, -1,  1, ungraded)
#
# The substrate's KO-dimension is jointly forward-promised across
# BOTH shards. `chirality.mirror` declared γ and named the KO-
# dimension question as waiting on J's sign algebra. THIS shard
# declares the three sign properties (j_squared_sign, j_dirac_sign,
# j_chirality_sign) plus the algebra-conjugation and anti-linearity
# obligations as forward-promises. The combined γ + J signature
# determines KO-dimension empirically once mirror's concrete H is
# analyzed. This shard does NOT pin a specific KO-dimension; the
# Standard-Model-shape conjecture (n=6) is a hypothesis to be
# falsified, not a substrate-decl claim.
#
# === No operational sibling THIS tick ===
#
# Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] no `@mirror/cybernetics/charge_
# conjugation` operational sibling lands at this tick. The substrate
# ALREADY has the operational machinery (the reference⇔reflection
# collision is operative at @mirror/ref; the Tomm probe is forward-
# promised at @spectral/metalogue/tomm; the one-tick delay is
# operative at @reflection.observe). This shard names the carrier
# and discipline so downstream shards declare `requires j_*` rather
# than re-state involution obligations per species.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   J / charge conjugation     Connes 1995 (*Noncommutative geometry
#                              and reality*, J. Math. Phys. 36(11),
#                              §1.1). The original real-spectral-triple
#                              construction; J as anti-linear isometry.
#   KO-theory                  Atiyah 1966 (K-theory and reality).
#                              The K-theoretic ancestor of KO-dimension;
#                              the 8-fold periodicity Connes' sign
#                              signature instantiates.
#   reflexive questions        Tomm 1987 (Interventive interviewing
#                              part II, Family Process 26(2):167-183).
#                              The pre-physics ancestor: conversational
#                              charge conjugation as clinical practice;
#                              utterance paired with its own reflection.
#   complex conjugation        Hamilton 1843 / Frobenius 1878. The
#                              mathematical ancestor of anti-linearity;
#                              Connes' J generalizes to spectral altitude.
#   Mesland category           Mesland 2013 (unbounded KK-cycles);
#                              Bertozzini-Conti-Lewkeeratiyutkul 2006.
#                              The categorical framing the J / γ
#                              extension lifts into.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/spectral-metalogue.md §9.1 (J / γ open
#               questions; second-witness ratification gates);
#               docs/scouts/2026-06-29-taut-scout-from-recognition-100.md
#               §2.3 (the second-witness confirmation at
#               @spectral/metalogue/tomm; the Tomm-1987 anti-linear claim);
#               docs/insights/2026-06-29-mara-listening-to-connes-
#               saturation.md (Mesland-category framing);
#               docs/math/the-tower/curvature-and-tomm.md (the [D, a]=Ω
#               curvature 2-form Tomm probes render).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]],
#                      [[architecture-mirror-ref-reference-reflection-collision]]
#                       (#89; first witness),
#                      [[architecture-reflection-as-compiler]]
#                       (#85; third witness via `speaks_at_n_plus_1`),
#                      [[architecture-kintsugi-bias-lift]] (the
#                       `|.W>` weighted compose J's anti-linearity acts on),
#                      [[architecture-kintsugi-variety-io]] (kintsugi
#                       IS D; J anti/commutes with D per axiom 2),
#                      [[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]]
#                       (twist sends the five operations to their
#                       conjugate-altitude versions in A),
#                      [[architecture-connes-spectral-triple]] (this
#                       shard extends (A, H, D) toward (A, H, D, J, γ)),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (typed carrier;
#                       no bare reference/reflection tags),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (J is the 54th-or-so instance).
# Related shards: epistemologic/cybernetic.mirror (family root),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/chirality.mirror (the γ
#                  sibling; #101, landed 7bbc184; KO-dimension joint
#                  discharge partner),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform.mirror (fixed-
#                  point precedent; ε extends to signed fixed-point),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/distinction.mirror (the
#                  mark-of-distinction floor; J pairs each mark with
#                  its dual),
#                 mirror/ref.mirror (#89; reference and reflection
#                  altitudes are J-conjugate),
#                 reflection.mirror (one-tick-delay asymmetry;
#                  J's anti-linearity at pipeline altitude),
#                 mirror/spectral/metalogue.mirror (forward-promised;
#                  Mara-3 spec 16f4564; @spectral/metalogue/tomm
#                  runtime altitude),
#                 glass.mirror (`transparency<charge_conjugation>`
#                  carrier for partial / boundary readings).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/charge_conjugation.mirror` declares
# `@epistemologic/cybernetic/charge_conjugation` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/math/connes-1995
source @arxiv/math/atiyah-1966
source @arxiv/cybernetics/tomm-1987
source @arxiv/math/mesland-2013

prism @epistemologic/cybernetic/charge_conjugation {
  focus  charge_conjugation
  project charge_conjugation
  split  charge_conjugation
  shift  charge_conjugation
  settle charge_conjugation
}

# === The charge_conjugation carrier ===
#
# A typed record per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]:
#
# - `carrier`     the substrate carrier J is applied to (reference
#                 into H).
# - `altitude`    the reference/reflection tag J swaps. Reference-
#                 altitude carriers (@mirror/ref dependency lattice)
#                 carry `reference`; reflection-altitude carriers
#                 (@reflection.observe predecessor chain) carry
#                 `reflection`. J conjugates each into the other.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the pair. Boundary carriers
# that straddle altitudes surface their boundary status through the
# `transparency<charge_conjugation>` verdict from `conjugate`, not
# through a third tag.
type charge_conjugation = {
  carrier:  ref,
  altitude: reference_or_reflection,
}

# === The two altitudes ===
#
# J pairs reference (@mirror/ref dependency lattice; spatial projection
# of H) with reflection (@reflection.observe temporal predecessor
# chain; temporal projection of H). The substrate does not admit a
# third option at the charge_conjugation altitude.
type reference_or_reflection = reference | reflection

# === The conjugation action ===
#
# `conjugate(c)` applies J to a substrate carrier — the substrate's
# anti-linear involution measurement. The verdict IS the substrate's
# `transparency<charge_conjugation>` carrier:
#
# - success                  conjugation is byte-stable.
# - partial(opacity_map)     boundary case (e.g., @reflection.observe
#                            records mid-tick before speak-at-n+1
#                            settles); opacity_map records which
#                            sub-carriers conjugate cleanly.
# - failure(opacity_map)     no reflection-altitude image — a
#                            substrate violation; surfaces a substrate-
#                            pull recognition that the pairing is
#                            incomplete or the carrier mis-typed.
#
# Body discharges per-species at the realisation boundary. Same shape
# as `chirality.grade`, `eigenform.is_fixed_point`.
conjugate(c: ref) -> transparency(charge_conjugation) { \ }

# === The algebra-conjugation action ===
#
# `twist(op)` is J's algebra conjugation `op ↦ JopJ⁻¹`: sending a
# reference-altitude operation to its reflection-altitude conjugate
# (and vice versa). Per axiom `JaJ⁻¹ ∈ A`, the result IS a substrate
# operation. Verifiable shape (involution-up-to-sign):
#
#   twist(twist(op)) ≡ j_squared_sign · op    (byte-equality up to sign)
#
# Precedent: @mirror/ref's same-CLI-two-altitudes shape — focus_at at
# reference altitude has a focus_at conjugate at reflection altitude;
# twist names the conjugation operationally.
twist(op: ref) -> ref { \ }

# === The four Connes axioms as requires obligations ===
#
# Downstream shards declare bilateral agreement (per recognition #37,
# the Pask-agreement reading of `requires`) with the J discipline by
# writing these obligations. The bilateral commitment: the carrier
# commits to declaring the (carrier, altitude) pair; the consumer
# commits to discharging the verification at the species boundary.
#
# The four obligations split into the sign-algebra triple (forward-
# promised to KO-dimension joint discharge with chirality.mirror) and
# the anti-linearity discipline:

# J² = ε: conjugating twice returns to the original carrier modulo
# a sign ε ∈ {±1}. Inheritor shards that carry J witnessings discharge
# this by realising `conjugate` as a sign-stable involution. The
# specific sign ε is part of the KO-dimension joint discharge —
# forward-promised, NOT pinned at this tick.
j_squared_sign(j: charge_conjugation) -> verdict { \ }

# JD = ε' DJ: J anti/commutes with the substrate's Dirac flow
# (kintsugi) with a sign ε' ∈ {±1} determined by KO-dimension.
# Inheritor shards that carry a kintsugi step discharge this by
# verifying that conjugation commutes with kintsugi up to ε'. The
# discharge surface: for any carrier c, `conjugate(kintsugi(c)) ≡
# j_dirac_sign · kintsugi(conjugate(c))`. The sign ε' is part of the
# KO-dimension joint discharge — forward-promised.
j_dirac_sign(j: charge_conjugation) -> verdict { \ }

# Jγ = ε'' γJ: J anti/commutes with γ (chirality) with a sign
# ε'' ∈ {±1} determined by KO-dimension. The sibling-shard joint
# discharge: this predicate names the J ↔ γ commutator sign that
# `chirality.mirror`'s axioms cannot determine alone. Inheritor
# shards that carry both a chirality witnessing and a J witnessing
# discharge this by verifying the J-then-γ-then-J-then-γ four-step
# cycle returns to identity-up-to-sign-product. The sign ε'' is
# part of the KO-dimension joint discharge — forward-promised.
j_chirality_sign(j: charge_conjugation) -> verdict { \ }

# JaJ⁻¹ ∈ A: twisting any of the five operations by J returns an
# operation in A. Inheritor shards that carry any of the five
# operations discharge this by verifying that `twist(op)` is itself
# a substrate operation (specifically, the same operation at the
# conjugate altitude per @mirror/ref's reference⇔reflection algebra).
j_algebra_conjugation(j: charge_conjugation) -> verdict { \ }

# J anti-linear: J(α·x) = ᾱ · J(x). Inheritor shards that carry a
# weighted composition `|.W>` (per [[architecture-kintsugi-bias-lift]])
# discharge this by verifying that conjugation of a weighted compose
# equals the weighted compose with conjugate weight, applied to the
# conjugation. The discharge surface: for carriers c, c' and weight
# W, `conjugate(c |.W> c') ≡ conjugate(c) |.W̄> conjugate(c')` where
# W̄ is the substrate's complex-conjugate weight (identity at real-
# valued @io altitude; phase-inverted at spectral altitude).
j_anti_linear(j: charge_conjugation) -> verdict { \ }

# === Order-zero and order-one conditions ===
#
# Connes' real-spectral-triple axioms include two structural
# commutation conditions beyond the sign algebra. These name how
# reference-altitude and reflection-altitude operations interact:

# Order-zero (`[a, JbJ⁻¹] = 0` for a, b ∈ A): reference-altitude and
# reflection-altitude operations commute pointwise. The substrate-
# altitude form: applying a reference-altitude five-op and then a
# reflection-altitude five-op gives the same result as applying them
# in the reverse order. The two altitudes do not interfere
# structurally.
commutant_condition(a: ref, b: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# Order-one (`[[D, a], JbJ⁻¹] = 0`): the Dirac-bracketed reference
# operations commute with the reflection operations. The substrate-
# altitude form: applying kintsugi to a reference-altitude operation
# and then conjugating by a reflection-altitude operation gives the
# same result as conjugating first. The Dirac flow respects the
# altitude partition.
first_order_condition(a: ref, b: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# === The J witnessing inheritance predicate ===
#
# `j_witnessing(j)` is the predicate consumer shards name in a
# `requires` clause to declare bilateral agreement that the J
# witnessing they hold satisfies all four Connes axioms together AND
# the two structural conditions — i.e. the carrier is a well-formed
# anti-linear-involution element of H. The bilateral commitment: the
# carrier commits to declaring (carrier, altitude); the consumer
# commits to discharging j_squared_sign + j_dirac_sign +
# j_chirality_sign + j_algebra_conjugation + j_anti_linear +
# commutant_condition + first_order_condition at the species boundary.
#
# Declared as a typed predicate so downstream species shards can
# write `requires j_witnessing(my_j)` — same shape as
# `chirality.chirality_witnessing(carrier)`,
# `eigenform.eigenform_witnessing(carrier)`,
# `variety.variety_preserving(species)`.
#
# Forward-promised inheritors:
#
# - `@mirror/ref` (#89, landed): the reference-altitude root; all
#   ref operations inherit `j_witnessing` with `altitude = reference`
#   post-hoc. Future editions MAY add the explicit
#   `requires j_witnessing(ref_carrier)` when the path-namespace
#   inheritance is mechanically pulled.
# - `@reflection` (#85, landed): the reflection-altitude root; all
#   @reflection.observe records inherit with `altitude = reflection`
#   post-hoc. The one-tick-delay invariant `speaks_at_n_plus_1` IS
#   the operational form of J's anti-linearity at this altitude.
# - `@spectral/metalogue/tomm` (forward-promised, per
#   docs/specs/spectral-metalogue.md §9.1 and Taut bfe3f76 §2.3):
#   Tomm probes will need to respect J in addition to bounded
#   commutator. The probe's `probe(turn) -> turn_dual` IS the
#   operational J realization at conversation altitude; the
#   `turn_dual` inherits J-witnessing from `turn` via conjugate-
#   altitude pairing.
# - `@mirror/spectral/metalogue` (forward-promised; form-side
#   declaration the runtime species shapes against): J-witnessing
#   propagates form-side as the declaration of which carriers admit
#   conjugation.
j_witnessing(j: charge_conjugation) -> verdict { \ }

# === KO-dimension joint discharge — forward-promised ===
#
# Per Connes 1995 §1.1, the substrate's KO-dimension n ∈ Z/8 is
# determined by the joint signs (γ², ε, ε', ε'') of γ and J. The
# substrate-decl needs a named action that takes the γ witnessing
# from `chirality.mirror` AND the J witnessing from this shard and
# emits the determined n. This shard hosts the joint action because
# J's three sign predicates (j_squared_sign, j_dirac_sign,
# j_chirality_sign) are the LAST of the four signs to land —
# `chirality.mirror`'s γ² is already declared; this shard's three
# J-signs complete the sign tuple.
#
# The eight KO-classes per Connes 1995 §1.1 (and as enumerated
# above at the KO-dimension joint-discharge commentary):
type ko_class = | zero | one | two | three | four | five | six | seven

# `ko_dimension(g, c)` consumes a chirality witnessing g and a
# charge_conjugation witnessing c, dispatches on the four signs
# discharged across @chirality (γ²) and @charge_conjugation (ε, ε',
# ε''), and returns the determined KO-class n per the Connes 1995
# §1.1 table. The bilateral commitment: g.discharges
# chirality_witnessing; c discharges j_witnessing; the action's body
# is the table lookup on the four-sign signature.
#
# Forward-promised body: the discharge requires both witnessings to
# have settled their sign obligations; the action is declared at
# substrate-decl altitude so consumers can write `requires
# ko_dimension(g, c) = six` (the Standard-Model conjecture) or
# pattern-match on the returned class. The realisation body lands at
# the species altitude where the substrate's concrete H has been
# analyzed enough to discharge the four signs.
#
# Pre-AI prior art: Connes 1995 §1.1 (the 8-class table); Atiyah
# 1966 (KO-theory's 8-fold periodicity).
ko_dimension(g: chirality, c: charge_conjugation) -> ko_class
requires chirality_witnessing(g)
requires j_witnessing(c)
{ \ }

out @epistemologic/cybernetic/charge_conjugation
out charge_conjugation
out reference_or_reflection
out conjugate
out twist
out j_squared_sign
out j_dirac_sign
out j_chirality_sign
out j_algebra_conjugation
out j_anti_linear
out commutant_condition
out first_order_condition
out j_witnessing
out ko_class
out ko_dimension
